@* Страницата за рекордния сезон 73–9 на Golden State Warriors (2015–16) *@
@inject PhotoService Faces
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "73–9";
}
<section class="view">
    <div class="ghead"><div><div class="label">Record · 2015–16 Golden State Warriors</div><h2>73–9: the best season ever</h2><p>In 2015–16 the Golden State Warriors won 73 of their 82 games. No team has ever won more in one regular season. But the story has a twist: they did not win the title.</p></div></div>
    <div class="rc-facts"><div class="num"><b>73</b><span>wins</span></div><div class="num"><b>9</b><span>losses</span></div><div class="num"><b>24–0</b><span>start, best ever</span></div><div class="num"><b>39–2</b><span>at home</span></div><div class="num"><b>+10.8</b><span>points per game better than opponents</span></div></div>
    <div class="tm-box"><h3>The team</h3><div class="rc-players"><div class="rc-pl">@Faces.Face("Stephen Curry", "curryst01", "PG")<div><b>Stephen Curry</b> <small class="muted">PG</small><p>MVP, the first ever voted unanimously. 30.1 points per game and 402 three-pointers, the most ever in one season (his old record was 286).</p></div></div><div class="rc-pl">@Faces.Face("Klay Thompson", "thompkl01", "SG")<div><b>Klay Thompson</b> <small class="muted">SG</small><p>22.1 points per game and 276 threes. With Curry they were the “Splash Brothers”.</p></div></div><div class="rc-pl">@Faces.Face("Draymond Green", "greendr01", "PF")<div><b>Draymond Green</b> <small class="muted">PF</small><p>The engine of the defense. 14.0 points, 9.5 rebounds and 7.4 assists per game, with 13 triple-doubles.</p></div></div><div class="rc-pl">@Faces.Face("Andre Iguodala", "iguodan01", "SF")<div><b>Andre Iguodala</b> <small class="muted">SF</small><p>Came off the bench and guarded the other team&#x27;s best player. He was the 2015 Finals MVP.</p></div></div><div class="rc-pl">@Faces.Face("Harrison Barnes", "barneha02", "SF")<div><b>Harrison Barnes</b> <small class="muted">SF</small><p>The fifth starter: a forward who could shoot from outside and defend bigger players.</p></div></div><div class="rc-pl">@Faces.Face("Andrew Bogut", "bogutan01", "C")<div><b>Andrew Bogut</b> <small class="muted">C</small><p>The center. Protected the rim, set screens for the shooters and passed well for a big man.</p></div></div></div></div>
    <div class="tm-box"><h3>The season, step by step</h3><ol class="rc-time"><li><b>Oct 2015</b><span>The defending champions start the season without coach Steve Kerr, who is out after back surgery. His assistant Luke Walton takes over.</span></li><li><b>Dec 2015</b><span>24–0, the best start in NBA history. The first loss comes on December 12 in Milwaukee.</span></li><li><b>Jan 2016</b><span>Kerr comes back. Under Walton the team went 39–4.</span></li><li><b>Feb 27, 2016</b><span>In Oklahoma City, Curry makes a game-winner from 38 feet (about 11.5 meters) in overtime. It is his 12th three of the night, tying the NBA record.</span></li><li><b>Apr 1, 2016</b><span>Boston wins in Oakland and ends a streak of 54 regular-season home wins in a row.</span></li><li><b>Apr 13, 2016</b><span>Last game: 125–104 against Memphis for win number 73, one more than the 1995–96 Bulls. Curry scores 46. The same night Kobe Bryant scores 60 in his last game.</span></li></ol></div>
    <div class="tm-box"><h3>Who beat them</h3><p class="muted">Only 9 teams managed it, and they never lost two games in a row all season.</p><div class="tm-legends"><span>Bucks</span><span>Mavericks</span><span>Nuggets</span><span>Pistons</span><span>Trail Blazers</span><span>Lakers</span><span>Spurs</span><span>Celtics</span><span>Timberwolves</span></div></div>
    <div class="tm-box"><h3>The best records in NBA history</h3><div class="rc-chart"><div class="rc-row me"><span class="rc-name"><b>Golden State Warriors</b><small>2015–16</small></span><span class="rc-bar"><i style="width:100.0%;--tc:@Teams.Get("GSW").Color"></i></span><span class="rc-wl">73–9</span></div><div class="rc-row"><span class="rc-name"><b>Chicago Bulls</b><small>1995–96</small></span><span class="rc-bar"><i style="width:98.6%;--tc:@Teams.Get("CHI").Color"></i></span><span class="rc-wl">72–10 🏆</span></div><div class="rc-row"><span class="rc-name"><b>Chicago Bulls</b><small>1996–97</small></span><span class="rc-bar"><i style="width:94.5%;--tc:@Teams.Get("CHI").Color"></i></span><span class="rc-wl">69–13 🏆</span></div><div class="rc-row"><span class="rc-name"><b>Los Angeles Lakers</b><small>1971–72</small></span><span class="rc-bar"><i style="width:94.5%;--tc:@Teams.Get("LAL").Color"></i></span><span class="rc-wl">69–13 🏆</span></div><div class="rc-row"><span class="rc-name"><b>Philadelphia 76ers</b><small>1966–67</small></span><span class="rc-bar"><i style="width:93.2%;--tc:@Teams.Get("PHI").Color"></i></span><span class="rc-wl">68–13 🏆</span></div><div class="rc-row"><span class="rc-name"><b>Boston Celtics</b><small>1972–73</small></span><span class="rc-bar"><i style="width:93.2%;--tc:@Teams.Get("BOS").Color"></i></span><span class="rc-wl">68–14</span></div><div class="rc-row"><span class="rc-name"><b>Oklahoma City Thunder</b><small>2024–25</small></span><span class="rc-bar"><i style="width:93.2%;--tc:@Teams.Get("OKC").Color"></i></span><span class="rc-wl">68–14 🏆</span></div></div><p class="muted">🏆 = won the title that season.</p></div>
    <div class="tm-box rc-twist"><h3>The twist: no title</h3><p>In the playoffs they beat Houston and Portland, then came back from 1–3 down against Oklahoma City in the Western Conference Finals.</p><p>In the Finals they led Cleveland 3–1, but Draymond Green was suspended for Game 5 and LeBron James and Kyrie Irving won the last three games. In Game 7 LeBron blocked Iguodala&#x27;s layup and Irving hit a three in the last minute. It was the first time a team came back from 3–1 down in the Finals.</p><p>That summer Kevin Durant joined the Warriors, and they won the title in 2017 and 2018.</p></div>
    <div class="real"><h3>What it means for 82-0</h3><p>Even the best team ever lost 9 games, and against the Lakers, a team that won only 17 games that year. That is why 82–0 is so hard: every team can lose on any night.</p><a class="btn" asp-controller="Challenge" asp-action="Index" style="justify-self:start">Try 82-0 →</a></div>
</section>
